Summary: Implement status lifecycle on TH records in Swimlane

Type: Sub-task (parent: WM-13)

User story

As a detection engineer maintaining threat hunts in Swimlane, I want each TH record's Status to drive a defined lifecycle, so that it's always clear whether a hunt is being built, tested, awaiting client approval, approved or live, and so the rule only runs when it should.

Context

The parent story notes the full TH process would benefit from lifecycle tracking in Swimlane, and that a hunt should be fully documented before it's enabled. TH records already have Status and Rule Execution (Enable/Disable) fields, but today any status can be chosen at any time, with no checks and no record of who changed it.

Lifecycle:

	•	Build → Testing / Tuning → Pending Client Approval → Approved → Deployed to Production
	•	Client rejection: Pending Client Approval → Testing / Tuning
	•	Changes to a live rule: Deployed to Production → Testing / Tuning

Status	Meaning	Rule Execution
Build	Hunt being written	Disabled
Testing / Tuning	Rule runs to be tested or tuned	Enabled
Pending Client Approval	Full write-up with the client	Disabled
Approved	Client signed off, awaiting deployment	Disabled
Deployed to Production	Live	Enabled

Acceptance criteria

	•	☐ New TH records default to Build.
	•	☐ Rule Execution is read-only and set automatically from Status, per the table above.
	•	☐ Whenever Status changes, Status Updated By (Swimlane user) and Status Updated On (date/time) are stamped automatically. Both fields are read-only.
	•	☐ Required fields are enforced per status:
	•	☐ Testing / Tuning: Execution Environment, Threat Hunt Type, Query Details
	•	☐ Pending Client Approval: the above, plus Use Case Summary, Desired Alert Conditions, Investigation Steps
	•	☐ Save is blocked when a required field for the selected status is empty.
	•	☐ In Approved and Deployed to Production, all content fields are read-only: Title, Execution Environment, Threat Hunt Type, Query Details, Use Case Summary, Desired Alert Conditions, Investigation Steps, Escalation Conditions, Known Tuning Exceptions, Severity Details and Audit.
	•	☐ In Approved and Deployed to Production, Status, Associated CIM Records and Reviews remain editable.
	•	☐ Moving a record from Deployed to Production back to Testing / Tuning makes its fields editable again.
	•	☐ Workflow branches using old status values (Draft, Aproved, Pending Client Review, Production Active, Tuning Needed) are removed or updated.
	•	☐ Existing TH records with an empty Status are given one.

Other information

	•	Implemented with Swimlane workflow only (conditions on Status, plus Set Value, Set Required and Set Read/Write actions). No new playbook.
	•	Only the latest status change is stamped on the record. The full change history is available in Swimlane record history.
	•	Enforcing the order of transitions (for example, blocking a jump from Build straight to Deployed) is out of scope for this sub-task and can be a follow-up.
	•	Testing / Tuning enables the rule because it has to run to be tested. Revisit this if testing happens outside Swimlane.
